{
  "dom_id": "step-q6785",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192268/assets/0f123b77781ae6c6665482418480605e8c61455d637dd92b8c929fa8ace7da3e.png)\n\nWhat is the domain of the function given above?",
  "worked_solution": "The function above is defined for values between $x=1$ and $x=4.$\n\n- Since there is a closed circle at $x=1,$ this point is included in the domain.\n\n- Since there is a closed circle at $x=4,$ this point is also included in the domain.\n\nTherefore, the domain of this function is\n\n$$\n1\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\nUsing interval notation, we can write this as\n\n$$\nx\\in [1,4].\n$$",
